These nodes contain no third-party source code and no model weights. They run on
ComfyUI's own native Marigold V2 support (the see-through loader decodes its 4-bit
nf4 backbone in plain PyTorch) and use the following works, which are installed
separately and keep their own licenses:

- Marigold V2 (huawei-bayerlab) - Apache License 2.0
  Code:    https://github.com/huawei-bayerlab/marigold-v2
  Weights: https://huggingface.co/huawei-bayerlab/marigold-v2-0

- Qwen-Image-Edit-2509 (Qwen team, Alibaba) - Apache License 2.0
  The backbone model Marigold V2 runs on.

- Marigold V2 see-through model files for ComfyUI - Apache License 2.0
  https://huggingface.co/Vathography/marigold-v2-see-through-comfyui
  Converted from Marigold V2 (depth/Log-layered) and Qwen-Image-Edit-2509.

- ComfyUI (Comfy Org) - GNU General Public License v3.0
  Native Marigold V2 nodes and model loading.

- kornia - Apache License 2.0
  Python dependency (already part of a standard ComfyUI install).

The hand photograph in assets/ (decoy_hand.png and the .npz files built
from it) is the author's own and is part of this software.
